# OpenPass — environment overview
#
# OpenPass is zero-knowledge: NO component needs (or should ever receive) your
# master password, vault keys, or item contents via environment variables.
# Each component has its own .env.example with details:
#
#   services/api/.env.example      Cloudflare Worker (the only server component)
#   apps/web/.env.example          Web vault (Vite build-time vars)
#   apps/extension/.env.example    Browser extension (no runtime env — by design)
#   apps/macos/.env.example        macOS app (no runtime env — build shell vars only)
#   apps/android/.env.example      Android app (build-time vars via Gradle/BuildConfig)
#   crates/openpass-core           Rust core: no environment variables at all
#
# Copy the relevant file to .env / .dev.vars as instructed inside it.
# Real env files are gitignored (.env, .env.*, .dev.vars); .env.example files are safe to commit.
# NEVER commit a filled-in .env with real secrets.
